soma-fluxvla is a focused derivative of FluxVLA by Limx Dynamics.
The retained training/model code originates from the sibling fluxvla-training
snapshot. Original copyright, license and embedded upstream attribution remain
in retained files. See LICENSE and source-manifest.json for source-file hashes.

Some retained files have individual upstream origin/license notices, including
OpenVLA-derived runner/logging code. Those notices are retained in their files.
The project package name is soma-fluxvla; its Python import namespace remains
fluxvla for compatibility with existing configuration and model checkpoints.

SOMA changes: training-only package registration, portable Piper configuration,
explicit predecoded cache integration, cache lifecycle validation and tooling.

Additional SOMA integration: canonical two-stage subtask pipeline, portable full-state
exports, shared physical-unit inference, cache fixes and text transition gating.

FAST assets under assets/fast originate from Physical Intelligence's FAST repository:
https://huggingface.co/physical-intelligence/fast (Apache-2.0 per its model card).
The local processor includes Transformers compatibility changes. Asset hashes are
recorded in assets/fast/SHA256SUMS. Base PI0.5 weights are not redistributed.
